{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "נצבים", :translit "nitzavim", :gloss "you stand"} {:he "ויתיצבו בתחתית ההר", :translit "va-yityatzvu be-tachtit ha-har", :gloss "and they stationed themselves at the foot of the mountain"} {:he "אתם נצבים", :translit "atem nitzavim", :gloss "you stand"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah: shared root נצב linking this verse to Sinai"}], :frame {:text "The verb ניצב (stationed) links Israel's covenant renewal here to the original revelation. The Talmud derives from ויתיצבו בתחתית ההר (Exodus 19:17) that the Israelites were coerced into accepting the Torah at Sinai (Shabbat 88a). The Ba'al HaTurim draws a verbal parallel between that Sinai stationing and the language of our verse, אתם נצבים היום כולכם (Deuteronomy 29:9), suggesting this assembly recapitulates the Sinai standing.", :sources ["Exodus 19:17" "Deuteronomy 29:9" "Shabbat 88a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לפני ה' אל", :translit "lifnei Hashem El", :gloss "before YHWH El"} {:he "ראשיכם", :translit "rasheichem", :gloss "your heads"} {:he "הקיש ראשיכם לאלהיכם", :translit "heikish rasheichem le-elohaychem", :gloss "He juxtaposed your heads to your Elohim"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhut ha-parashot: proximity of 'your heads' to the divine name"}], :frame {:text "The phrase לפני ה' אלהיכם (Deuteronomy 29:9) is immediately followed by ראשיכם שבטיכם. This juxtaposition yields the principle מורא רבך כמורא שמים, the fear of your teacher is like the fear of Heaven. The Talmud derives this from the verse את ה' אלהיך תירא (Deuteronomy 6:13), read as את ואת ה' אלהיך תירא — to include scholars alongside God (Pesachim 22b). The same principle is restated in the Talmud's instruction that a student's awe of his teacher should parallel awe of Heaven (Avodah Zarah 19a).", :sources ["Deuteronomy 29:9" "Deuteronomy 6:13" "Pesachim 22b" "Avodah Zarah 19a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ישראל", :translit "Yisrael", :gloss "Israel"} {:he "וסמיך ליה", :translit "u-semikh lei", :gloss "and adjacent to it"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhut ha-parashot: adjacency of 'Israel' to the next word, pointing to what follows"}], :frame nil}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah: shared root נצב linking this verse to Sinai", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Semikhut ha-parashot: proximity of 'your heads' to the divine name", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Semikhut ha-parashot: adjacency of 'Israel' to the next word, pointing to what follows", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:40:16.817452750Z", :model "glm-5.2"}